 "title": "County Recorder – Mitchell County, IA",
 "text": "County Recorder – Mitchell County, IA\nSkip to content\nSkip to main navigation\nSkip to footer\n641-832-3946\n212 S. 5th St, Osage, IA - MAP\n8:00am - 4:30pm Monday - Friday\nEmployment Opportunities\nAgendas / Proceedings\nPublic Notices\nHome\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAttorney\nAuditor\nBoard of Supervisors\nClerk of Court\nE-911\nEconomic Development\nEmergency Management\nEngineer\nEnvironmental Health\nGIS\nConservation\nHuman Services\nIT / Maintenance\nMotor Vehicle\nPlanning & Zoning\nProperty Taxes\nPublic Health\nRecorder\nRecycling Center\nSheriff’s Department\nGeneral Assistance\nTreasurer\nVeterans Affairs\nVoting\nContact\nHow Do I...\nParcel Data\nGIS/Mapping\nHome\nDepartments\nCounty Recorder\nMitchell County Recorder: Hannah Elliott\n(641) 832-3941 ext. 107 – EMAIL\nStaff:\nMonica Sigler (641) 832-3941 ext. 108 – EMAIL\nCounty Recorder Documents |\nBirth Certificate Replacement |\nBoat Application -DNR Form 542-8067 |\nMilitary Discharge Information |\nMarriage Instructions |\nThe Recorder’s Office was created in 1839 by the First Legislative Assembly. The Recorder continues to maintain official records of documents affecting title to real estate. Every real estate transaction that takes place begins in the Recorder’s Office. One of the major duties of the office is the management of public records. As a result, accuracy and preservation of records are a must in the Recorder’s Office. Instruments that are recorded are not only important for today, but serve as a historical library for all of the tomorrows.\nIn addition to real estate transactions, the Recorder’s Office issues titles and liens; records veterans discharge papers; takes passport pictures; accepts marriage applications and issues the subsequent license; issues certified copies of birth, death and marriage records as well as other numerous duties.\nBirth Records from 1880\nDeath Records from 1880\nMarriage Records from 1855\nLand Records from 1854 — beginning of the county\nAdditional Resources\nwww.IowaLandRecords.org – source for information about recorded real estate documents in Iowa.\nCONTACT INFO\n8:00am – 4:30pm Mon-Fri\n212 S. 5th St.\nOsage, IA 50461 | MAP\nPhone: (641) 832-3941\nVisit Us on Facebook\nHannah Elliott\nMitchell County Recorder\nEMAIL\n(641) 832-3941 ext. 107\nUpcoming Events\nThere are no posts\nMonica Sigler\nMitchell County Recorder Office\nMitchell County Courthouse\n212 S. 5th St.\nOsage, IA 50461\n(641) 832-3946\nMonday - Friday 8:00am to 4:30pm\nMitchell County Courthouse Holiday Schedule\nPhone Numbers\nMitchell County Assessor\n(641) 832-3945 ext. 113\nMitchell County Auditor\n(641) 832-3946 ext. 101\nMitchell County Treasurer\n(641) 832-3940\nConservation\n(641) 732-5204\nEconomic Development\n(641) 732-4790\nSee All Phone Numbers\nMitchell County, IA\n© 2026 Mitchell County Iowa Courthouse\n&placement=right&parentOrigin=https://mitchellcounty.iowa.gov&mobile=0\" style=\"width: 255px; height: 253.453px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; position: fixed; right: 20px; left: unset; bottom: 60px; z-index: 10000;\">",
